# Auth, Route Protection & Error Boundaries

## 1. Route Layouts
- `src/routes/auth/` — unauthenticated screens (login, forgot/reset password).
  Layout is the centered card shell.
- `src/routes/dashboard/` — everything behind login; wrapped by
  `DashboardShell`. Assume an authenticated user in these components.
- New authed screens go under `dashboard/`; new public/auth screens under `auth/`.

## 2. Route Guard
- Protect dashboard routes with a `<RequireAuth>` wrapper (or a React Router
  loader that checks the session) in the route tree — **not** Vite middleware.
- No session → `navigate` to `/:locale/login` (locale-aware), preserving the
  intended path as a return-to query when useful.
- Logged-in users hitting auth screens → redirect into the dashboard.

## 3. Token Handling
- Access token lives in memory (module singleton + context), refreshed via a
  refresh token in an httpOnly cookie (set/rotated by the backend). Don't put
  the access token in `localStorage`.
- The API client attaches it to every request and handles refresh-on-401
  (@api-client.md §2).
- On a hard `401` (refresh failed): clear session once, navigate to `/login`,
  and drop the React Query cache (`queryClient.clear()`).

## 4. Current User
- One `useCurrentUser()` hook backed by a long `staleTime` query
  (`userKeys` / `authKeys.me`). Gate role-specific UI on its data — never on a
  value duplicated into component state.

## 5. Error & Not-Found
- Shared `errorElement` on the auth layout and the dashboard layout (reset
  button, generic translated message — no stack traces).
- Dashboard errors render **inside** the shell so nav stays usable; auth errors
  use the plain card shell.
- Route-level skeletons (`create-loading-skeletons` skill) cover first paint
  and `isLoading`.
- Expected data errors surface as inline states from hooks; reserve the route
  error boundary for render-time / unexpected failures.

## 6. Firebase / Notifications
- `firebase` here is for FCM push (the `notifications` feature), not the auth
  provider. Don't wire Firebase Auth unless explicitly asked.
